==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{affix|ru|врать|-ач}}. Originally meant "witch-doctor, enchanter".

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|Ru-врач.ogg|Audio|lang=ru}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|b|a=an}}

# [[physician]], [[doctor]]

====Usage notes====
A female medical doctor is referred to as '''врач''', or [[женщина]]-врач, or, colloquially only, [[врачиха]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ru|до́ктор}}
* {{l|ru|знахарь}}
* {{l|ru|ле́карь}}
* {{l|ru|целитель}}

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-table|b|a=an}}
Note: There is an archaic vocative {{m|ru|вра́чу}}.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ru|врачебный}}
* {{l|ru|врачевание}}
* {{l|ru|врачевать}}
* {{l|ru|врачи́ха}}
* {{l|ru|врачующий}}

[[Category:ru:Medicine]]

